# Admin panel

`/admin` is an internal tool, not part of the public TH/EN site. No `lib/i18n`
dictionaries, no `[locale]` layout, excluded from locale-redirect middleware.

## Firestore is Admin SDK only

Public pages and `/admin` both read/write Firestore via `firebase-admin` in Server
Components and Route Handlers (`lib/firebase/admin.ts`). The browser never talks to
Firestore. `firestore.rules` stays deny-all. Do not add the client Firestore SDK.

## Auth

Firebase Auth email/password (client SDK in `lib/firebase/client.ts`, Auth only) mints
an ID token; `POST /api/admin/session` verifies it against `ADMIN_ALLOWED_EMAILS` and
sets an httpOnly session cookie (`lib/admin/session.ts`). Guard writes in route
handlers and `/admin/blog/layout.tsx` — never a top-level `/admin` layout, or login
becomes unreachable.

## Blog posts

`parsePost()` in `lib/blog/parse-post.ts` is the single validator for JSON files,
Firestore reads, and admin form submissions. Do not add a second parser or `zod`.
Writes go through route handlers (`runtime = "nodejs"`, `dynamic = "force-dynamic"`,
`{ ok: boolean }`), then `revalidateTag(BLOG_POSTS_TAG)`.
